cff-version: 1.2.0
title: BinderCyte
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: van Warmerdam
    given-names: Travis C.
    affiliation: The Pennsylvania State University
abstract: >-
  Two local graphical tools for the front half of a de novo protein binder
  design campaign. The first loads a target structure, builds a per-residue
  inventory with chemistry classes and pairwise hotspot distances, and exports
  a cropped, renumbered target with a validated hotspot string. The second
  configures the design campaign, generates a manifest and a SLURM array
  script, and transfers and submits the job over SSH.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-05"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tvanwar11/BinderCyte"
license: MIT
